## int_jira__issue_assign_resolution

    - name: int_jira__issue_assign_resolution
      description: First and last assignment timestamps and first resolution timestamp per issue.
      grain: One row per issue_id
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__issue_field_history
      business_logic: '- Start from intermediate.int_jira__issue_field_history. - Keep rows where field_id equals "assignee" or "resolutiondate" when compared case-insensitively, and field_value is not null. - For each issue_id, compute: - first_assigned_at: the earliest updated_at among rows whose field_id equals the lowercase string "assignee" exactly (case-sensitive match to the literal); result is null if none qualify. - last_assigned_at: the latest updated_at among rows whose field_id equals the lowercase string "assignee" exactly (case-sensitive match to the literal); result is null if none qualify. - first_resolved_at: the earliest updated_at among rows whose field_id equals the lowercase string "resolutiondate" exactly (case-sensitive match to the literal); result is null if none qualify. - Aggregate functions ignore null updated_at values; duplicate source rows are not deduplicated. - No joins, ordering, timezone normalization, truncation, or rounding are applied. - Output includes one row for each issue_id present in the filtered data.'
      columns:
      - name: issue_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Issue key used to group rows; one row per issue_id in the filtered data.
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: first_assigned_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Earliest updated_at among filtered rows with field_id exactly 'assignee'; null if none.
      - name: last_assigned_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Latest updated_at among filtered rows with field_id exactly 'assignee'; null if none.
      - name: first_resolved_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Earliest updated_at among filtered rows with field_id exactly 'resolutiondate'; null if none.


